{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/8069","id":5233462026,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABN_BLCg","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8069","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8069.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8069.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8069","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/8069/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/8069/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8069/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/ee358553e4474c59f5fc4b54a8ec12940fda1985","number":8069,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(fleet-dispatch): checked arithmetic on peer-declared chunk size in dechunked_len (#6512)","user":{"login":"developing-today[bot]","id":347365078,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOFLRe1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\n`dechunked_len` (fleet-dispatch's chunked-response completeness checker) did raw arithmetic on the peer-declared chunk size: `size + 2` for the completeness guard and the slice index, `total += size` for the running total. For a chunk-size line naming `usize::MAX` or `usize::MAX - 1` that panics in debug builds and wraps in release builds, so the completeness verdict is computed from wrapped values (#6512; the #5579 rule — peer-declared sizes are never trusted).\n\n## Fix\n\nProduction code, not just the test: every arithmetic step on the declared size is now checked.\n\n- `size.checked_add(2)` — a size whose chunk + trailing CRLF cannot fit a `usize` reads as \"not complete\" (`None`).\n- The guard compares the buffered remainder against that checked end.\n- `total.checked_add(size)` — the running total is checked too.\n- The slice advances by the checked end.\n\nA chunk-size line that cannot describe a body within the buffered remainder is therefore \"not complete\" in every profile — never a panic, never a completed body computed from wrapped values. Signature and caller contract unchanged; `dechunk` (already guarded) untouched.\n\n## Test\n\nThe characterization test salvaged from PR #7524 pinned the old overflow-panic (\"must overflow-panic on usize::MAX until #6512 lands\") and failed deterministically in the release-profile Nix check phase, blocking every generation build from `main`. It is updated deliberately, as its own comment instructed, into `dechunked_len_huge_chunk_size_is_not_complete`, pinning:\n\n- both overflow sizes (`usize::MAX`, `usize::MAX - 1`) → `None` via direct calls (a panic would fail the test);\n- a huge declared size after a valid first chunk → `None`;\n- a large-but-plausible size (16 MiB) with insufficient bytes buffered → `None`;\n- the existing happy-path pins unchanged.\n\nVerified on the laptop, real crate:\n\n- `cargo test -p fleet-dispatch` (debug): 11 passed, 0 failed\n- `cargo test --release -p fleet-dispatch` (release): 11 passed, 0 failed\n\nFixes #6512. This also unblocks the #7991 deploy: fork PR opencode#2237 and pin bump #8067 are merged, but no generation could build from `main` while this check-phase failure stood.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796862058&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=8069&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F8069&signature=ec54d42daae88034769c34e0420d1ecb2f1dd2e19ed5bf765633692f5c72f8c8\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/8069?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-10T00:20:54Z","updated_at":"2026-11-14T21:53:38Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T00:22:26Z","merged_at":"2026-11-10T00:22:26Z","merge_commit_sha":"8f27f045e06b9073056aa31ca2c7ffa696c19cf0","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"